<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bursa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bursa is a city in northwestern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-marmara">Sea of Marmara</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osman-i">Osman I</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> emerged in the Bithynian borderlands near the city, and it was captured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1326. It became the first major capital of the Ottoman Empire and a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bursa.jpg" alt="Bursa" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Metuboy · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bursa_image.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
